"dmacwalter","author_id":"227752255","text":"@DrSdeG I’m sure yours was a typo, but I’m curious why everyone has used HPMV rather than HMPV in their replies. A quick google shows only GBnews and Daily Mail have used HPMV and even then not consistently.","in_corpus":true,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":18.349,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876808046992626130","x":0.508254,"y":28.0,"t":1736300882,"iso":"2025-01-08T01:48:02.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"Le077ne","author_id":"1696179398532071425","text":"@DrSdeG For peds they do a whole panel that would show it","in_corpus":false,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":9.989,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876796885362430322","x":0.470646,"y":27.0,"t":1736298221,"iso":"2025-01-08T01:03:41.000Z","rt":1,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":4,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"honeybeepetal","author_id":"263881113","text":"@DrSdeG @HeldinEU Worth getting pneumoniajab - diabetic, ticker &amp; mitochondrial disease, chronic fatigue? 51","in_corpus":false,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":1,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":9.25,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876760044022231184","x":0.346501,"y":26.0,"t":1736289437,"iso":"2025-01-07T22:37:17Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":4,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"BanjoBlood16","author_id":"1769768858393436160","text":"@DrSdeG It's on our extended panel. We don't seem to have seen much. More flu/RSV/paraflu/rhino. Some years it all seems to be metapneumovirus","in_corpus":true,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":6.81,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876737959044559181","x":0.27209,"y":25.0,"t":1736284172,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:09:32Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":4,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"surf4children","author_id":"3365662935","text":"@DrSdeG respiratory pcr panels ARE THE ONLY WAY TO BE SURE YOUR FLU IS EITHER FLU OR HMPV OR ANY OTHER VIRUS.\nall clinical diagnoses are just a guess","in_corpus":true,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":5.348,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876722313799901639","x":0.219374,"y":23.5,"t":1736280442,"iso":"2025-01-07T20:07:22.000Z","rt":9,"replies":2,"quotes":0,"likes":46,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"LongCovidHell","author_id":"1225382429080391680","text":"@DrSdeG I doubt they’re swabbing for anything in the NHS. Everything comes under “winter viruses” it seems. We’re screwed if bird flu hits. With no airborne measures and no testing, it’ll spread like wild fire.","in_corpus":false,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":9,"subtree_size":5,"dt_root_h":4.312,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876735854493807056","x":0.264995,"y":24.0,"t":1736283670,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:01:10.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":3,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"GeoWilding93","author_id":"28365943","text":"@LongCovidHell @DrSdeG We are 100% swabbing. Where I work full viral resp swab for anyone with a temp.","in_corpus":false,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":3,"dt_root_h":5.208,"parent_id":"1876722313799901639","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876743922770190350","x":0.292187,"y":24.0,"t":1736285594,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:33:14.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":3,"author":"LongCovidHell","author_id":"1225382429080391680","text":"@GeoWilding93 @DrSdeG Fantastic! For Covid too?","in_corpus":false,"depth":3,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":2,"dt_root_h":5.743,"parent_id":"1876735854493807056","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876744003179176407","x":0.292456,"y":24.0,"t":1736285613,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:33:33.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":1,"relation":"reply","niveau":4,"author":"GeoWilding93","author_id":"28365943","text":"@LongCovidHell @DrSdeG Yep does the full shebang.","in_corpus":false,"depth":4,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":5.748,"parent_id":"1876743922770190350","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876722995760120299","x":0.221663,"y":23.0,"t":1736280604,"iso":"2025-01-07T20:10:04.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":1,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"Oldboatie","author_id":"303350890","text":"@LongCovidHell @DrSdeG That’s what I thought but a couple of people have said they are swabbing which is good.","in_corpus":false,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":4.357,"parent_id":"1876722313799901639","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876704204401582286","x":0.158347,"y":21.5,"t":1736276124,"iso":"2025-01-07T18:55:24.000Z","rt":1,"replies":2,"quotes":0,"likes":6,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"fecklessfox1000","author_id":"1721174892698071040","text":"@DrSdeG Yes.  Respiratory infection gets a POCT to rule out Flu and then extended PCR panel including Covid, Flu A/B, Rhino/Entero , RSV, metapneomovirus and the other seasonal Coronavirus strains.","in_corpus":false,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":1,"subtree_size":3,"dt_root_h":3.112,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876720467232293361","x":0.213141,"y":22.0,"t":1736280001,"iso":"2025-01-07T20:00:01.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"a_rouquin","author_id":"998473145131700224","text":"@fecklessfox1000 @DrSdeG I’ve just had that bonkers RSV that’s going about  - four days in bed, five days hacking cough, another day of crazy temperatures and then three days of chrome orange snot. Which is nice","in_corpus":false,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":4.189,"parent_id":"1876704204401582286","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876707615956172958","x":0.169837,"y":21.0,"t":1736276937,"iso":"2025-01-07T19:08:57.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"JT91635781","author_id":"1116434351208718337","text":"@fecklessfox1000 @DrSdeG Is there checking for bird flu within that?","in_corpus":false,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":3.338,"parent_id":"1876704204401582286","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876694231340789772","x":0.124739,"y":20.0,"t":1736273746,"iso":"2025-01-07T18:15:46.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":3,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"RestedIn","author_id":"1427511061817831456","text":"@DrSdeG Had the flu + COVID vaccines ( so prob not them?)..\n Had something since last Sunday and it's hard going. Never known anything to last this long","in_corpus":false,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":3,"dt_root_h":2.452,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876754661845164290","x":0.328368,"y":20.0,"t":1736288154,"iso":"2025-01-07T22:15:54.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"HeldinEU","author_id":"891032413962457088","text":"@RestedIn @DrSdeG Hugs","in_corpus":false,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":2,"dt_root_h":6.454,"parent_id":"1876694231340789772","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876794854425919988","x":0.463805,"y":20.0,"t":1736297737,"iso":"2025-01-08T00:55:37.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":3,"author":"RestedIn","author_id":"1427511061817831456","text":"@HeldinEU @DrSdeG Why thank you!","in_corpus":false,"depth":3,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":9.116,"parent_id":"1876754661845164290","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876689720324816998","x":0.109545,"y":19.0,"t":1736272671,"iso":"2025-01-07T17:57:51.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":6,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"agemjourney","author_id":"1240338124619878402","text":"@DrSdeG We do when we do extended swabs, usually if flu etc are neg. Only seen one case on resp ward so far but loads of flu","in_corpus":false,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":1,"dt_root_h":2.153,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876685317056414010","x":0.094706,"y":17.5,"t":1736271621,"iso":"2025-01-07T17:40:21Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":2,"relation":"reply","niveau":1,"author":"Medicalis_UK","author_id":"777806323840905216","text":"@DrSdeG For care home respiratory outbreaks usually samples are tested for respiratory panel (flu a/b, parainfluenza, Covid, RSV, HMPV), hospital admissions also use similar multiplex panel","in_corpus":true,"depth":1,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":8,"dt_root_h":1.861,"parent_id":"1876657211499573570","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876733900099047453","x":0.258409,"y":17.5,"t":1736283204,"iso":"2025-01-07T20:53:24.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":1,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"sonia_chester","author_id":"3420316919","text":"@Medicalis_UK @DrSdeG No testing being done unless resident admitted in my experience. Patients with confirmed flu also being discharged to residential settings. Rarely see care home staff masking now. The IPC guidelines are so flawed @UKHSA","in_corpus":false,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":7,"dt_root_h":5.079,"parent_id":"1876685317056414010","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876735224144429080","x":0.262875,"y":17.5,"t":1736283520,"iso":"2025-01-07T20:58:40.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":3,"author":"Medicalis_UK","author_id":"777806323840905216","text":"@sonia_chester @DrSdeG @UKHSA suspected outbreaks are investigated and symptomatic patients are tested using multiplex resp panel.","in_corpus":false,"depth":3,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":6,"dt_root_h":5.167,"parent_id":"1876733900099047453","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876735647961973215","x":0.264303,"y":17.5,"t":1736283621,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:00:21.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":4,"author":"DrSdeG","author_id":"476562281","text":"@Medicalis_UK @sonia_chester @UKHSA Not happening locally - so wondering if it was anywhere else","in_corpus":false,"depth":4,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":5,"dt_root_h":5.195,"parent_id":"1876735224144429080","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876736024216277495","x":0.265561,"y":17.5,"t":1736283710,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:01:50.000Z","rt":0,"replies":2,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":5,"author":"Medicalis_UK","author_id":"777806323840905216","text":"@DrSdeG @sonia_chester @UKHSA Check with your local health protection team- it is happening in the SW.","in_corpus":false,"depth":5,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":4,"dt_root_h":5.219,"parent_id":"1876735647961973215","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876744314622976054","x":0.293502,"y":18.0,"t":1736285687,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:34:47.000Z","rt":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":6,"author":"sonia_chester","author_id":"3420316919","text":"@Medicalis_UK @DrSdeG @UKHSA Most nursing/care homes I’ve been to in last couple weeks have several residents with cough &amp; no swabs. Aware at least 2 nursing homes needing antivirals for flu following confirmed cases- all passed to 111/local GP’s to deal with. No public health prescribers managing outbreaks","in_corpus":false,"depth":6,"subtree_rt":0,"subtree_size":2,"dt_root_h":5.769,"parent_id":"1876736024216277495","conversation_id":"1876657211499573570"},{"id":"1876745368160866798","x":0.297049,"y":18.0,"t":1736285938,"iso":"2025-01-07T21:38:58.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":"reply","niveau":7,"author":"Medicalis_UK","author_id":"777806323840905216","text":"@sonia_chester @DrSdeG @UKHSA It’s not in public health/health protect